{
 "_doc": "The scenarios, in menu order (the battle console mockup's test scenes, owner 2026-11-04: \"make scenarios for both sides (concord and Krai)\"). Every scenario is the Krai Warhost against the Concord with the approved ships, no stand-ins (owner, 2026-11-04: \"NO PLACE HOLDERS SHOULD BE USED FOR KRAI VS CONCORD\"). side is the faction the player commands (its console skin is the faction's skin); the first ship is the player's. Positions in metres, heading in degrees clockwise from north (-z). Optional per ship, a captain's standing orders: stance (attack, escort, hold), range (close, mid, long), erratic, hold_fire, hull_frac, shields_frac. Battle is the mockup's Battle scene with the Krai line as the foe; Duel is one cruiser against one; Arming is the mockup's Arming scene without proximity torpedoes, which the game does not have yet. The Hunt (concord_hunt) puts the Ssarith Hunt's approved ships against the Concord (mockup 12; owner, 2026-11-06: \"looks good, implement in game\"); the Hunt is played as the Concord or the Krai there. Once the Hunt's console was built (mockup 15), the Ssarith are a side of their own (ssarith_battle, ssarith_duel, ssarith_arming: the Hunt's approved ships against the Concord's and the Krai's). The allied scenes (*_allied, *_four_races; the battle console mockup's Allied fleet and Four races, openspec/changes/fleet-skins) put a Concord, a Krai and a Ssarith ship in one fleet to hop between (the Fleet key, keys 1 to 9), the console wearing the skin of the ship you command; in them alone the foes are the mockup's Kethran and Vos stand-ins (no Krai or Concord stand-in anywhere), and Four races adds the Kelvane Institute's research cruiser Patience, a stand-in, the Institute having no designed ships, as the mockup does.",
